"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does conductivity-conditioned generation of disordered Li-halide electrolytes raise the hit rate for fast Li conductors over unconditioned generation as more candidates are screened?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Fine-tuning MatterGen's adapter on MLIP-predicted conductivity shifts generated halides toward fast Li conductors, because property conditioning already worked for bulk modulus [s_mattergen_5000].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mattergen_5000\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.03687v2\",\"quote\":\"Finally, we target structures with high bulk modulus—an important property for superhard materials. We fine-tune the model on only 5,000 labeled structures, and sample with a target value of 400 GPa.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"Conductivity labels feed adapter fine-tuning, then conditioned generation, screening, and NEB validation—five dependent steps.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"None—labels, generation, and screening are independent per structure and run side by side across GPUs.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"At 100,000 screened candidates the conditioned arm's hit rate exceeds unconditioned generation's, and the gap widens with candidate count [s_mattergen_saturate].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mattergen_saturate\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.03687v2\",\"quote\":\"While the number of structures found by screening saturates with increasing budget, MatterGen keeps discovering S.U.N. structures at an almost constant rate.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"The hit-rate gap between conditioned and unconditioned generation stays within seed-to-seed noise at every level, including 100,000 candidates.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Fine-tune MACE-MP-0b2 on DTU's 400k halide database, label with MD-predicted conductivity, fine-tune MatterGen's adapter, generate 1k/10k/100k candidates per arm, screen, NEB-validate top ten, compare hit rates.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"MatterGen's adapter fine-tuning shifted bulk-modulus generation toward extreme values with only 5,000 labels, but never conditioned on ionic conductivity or disordered halides.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mattergen_5000\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.03687v2\",\"quote\":\"Finally, we target structures with high bulk modulus—an important property for superhard materials. We fine-tune the model on only 5,000 labeled structures, and sample with a target value of 400 GPa.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No one has conditioned crystal generation on ionic conductivity for disordered halides, nor measured whether more candidates widens the conditioned hit-rate gap.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Reproduce MatterGen's 38.57% S.U.N. rate on 1,024 unconditional samples before trusting generation.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mattergen_sun\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mattergen/main/MODEL_CARD.md\",\"quote\":\"MatterGen achieves 38.57 % S.U.N. rate among generated structures\"}],\"value\":38.57}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows only MLIP-predicted conductivity, not DFT or measured; halide family only; no synthesis.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_mattergen_5000\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.03687v2\",\"quote\":\"Finally, we target structures with high bulk modulus—an important property for superhard materials. We fine-tune the model on only 5,000 labeled structures, and sample with a target value of 400 GPa.\",\"supports\":\"hypothesis: property conditioning works with few labels\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_mattergen_saturate\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.03687v2\",\"quote\":\"While the number of structures found by screening saturates with increasing budget, MatterGen keeps discovering S.U.N. structures at an almost constant rate.\",\"supports\":\"predictions.if_lever: the gap widens with candidate count\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_mattergen_sun\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mattergen/main/MODEL_CARD.md\",\"quote\":\"MatterGen achieves 38.57 % S.U.N. rate among generated structures\",\"supports\":\"anchor sun_rate = 38.57%\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:gen_rate\",\"name\":\"MatterGen sampling throughput\",\"value\":500,\"unit\":\"structure/GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"Sampling 1,000 structures takes around two hours using a single NVIDIA V100 GPU\",\"page_setting\":\"MatterGen base model, default settings, single V100 16GB\",\"differs_in\":[\"A6000 48GB instead of V100 16GB; A6000 is equal or faster, so 500/h is conservative\"],\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mattergen/main/MODEL_CARD.md\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:mace_step_ms\",\"name\":\"MACE step time\",\"value\":44.2,\"unit\":\"millisecond/step\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"quote\":\"MACE (large) | 2,139,152 | 1UAO | 6.3 ms/step | 11.6 ms/step | 44.2 ms/step\",\"page_setting\":\"MACE-large, 138-atom 1UAO system, Torch+ASE backend, single H100\",\"differs_in\":[\"A6000 48GB instead of H100\",\"200-atom halide supercell instead of 138-atom molecule\",\"MACE-MP-0b2-large instead of generic MACE-large\"],\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.22397v1\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:sun_rate\",\"name\":\"MatterGen unconditional S.U.N. rate\",\"value\":38.57,\"unit\":\"percent\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"MatterGen achieves 38.57 % S.U.N. rate among generated structures\",\"page_setting\":\"MatterGen unconditional generation, 1,024 samples\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/mattergen/main/MODEL_CARD.md\"}

